==Strategy==
Since there are no strong peons to support the Berserkories, you can easily defeat them by stacking [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] and simply overpowering them (possibly with the help of [[Cat Combo|Combos]]). Just make sure to quickly kill each of them to avoid fighting several Berserkories at once. For this task, strong [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red units]] such as [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Maximum the Fighter]] or [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] are recommended.

Alternatively, try bringing along the [[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!! Combo]] ([[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Marshmallow Cat (Rare Cat)|Creepmallow]]), [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] and [[Evil Cat (Rare Cat)|Gentleman Bros.]] If you time it correctly, every enemy in the level will be permanently frozen by a stack of Gentleman Bros. and Apple Cats, allowing you to kill them at your leisure. iCat, Apple's True Form, doesn't even need support from Gentleman Bros.

Another way to cheese the stage is to bring [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] or an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] alternative like [[Raiden (Uber Rare Cat)|Dragonslayer Raiden]] along. Just spam him (maybe with some "Research" Effect UP Combos) and, with good initial luck, the Berserkories will be unable to get close enough to attack. Of course, support is needed as the damage output would be quite low otherwise, possibly causing many Berserkories to stack.

One more strategy for this stage is using [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or another [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] to block the [[Wave Attack]]s while using Roe to weaken the Berserkories, then stacking attackers behind.

